int bc_debug_next(bc_client_t *c);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Steps execution to the next command at the same nesting depth, skipping
over function calls, subshells, and compound commands.
This is the \(lqstep over\(rq operation.
The function sends a \f[CR]next\f[R] command on \f[CR]CHAN_DEBUG\f[R]
(channel 4).
.PP
After stepping over, the debugger stops at the next command whose
nesting depth is less than or equal to the depth where \f[CR]next\f[R]
was issued.
Commands inside called functions or subshells execute without stopping.
.PP
