.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
\(lqSame depth\(rq means the execution nesting depth recorded when
\f[CR]next\f[R] was issued.
If the current command returns from a function (decreasing depth), the
debugger stops at the caller.
.IP \(bu 2
Breakpoints inside stepped\-over functions still fire.
Use \f[CR]bc_debug_continue()\f[R] if you want to skip breakpoints too
(note: continue does honor breakpoints; there is no \(lqrun ignoring
breakpoints\(rq command).
.IP \(bu 2
If the command at the current depth is the last in a block,
\f[CR]next\f[R] behaves like \f[CR]finish\f[R] for that block.
.IP \(bu 2
After \f[CR]bc_debug_next()\f[R], a new break\-hit event is generated
when the debugger stops.
Call \f[CR]bc_poll()\f[R] to receive it.
.IP \(bu 2
Thread safety: the client library is not thread\-safe.
